# 8. Marketplace and distribution

Matt asked to package this theme for sale. Follow 8.1–8.12 on marketplace work. README / `readme.txt` / ThemeForest documentation copy: `.cursor/rules/theme-shop-readme.mdc`.

This repo is still a **concept Sage theme**. Listings stay in-theme as a fallback so the live demo keeps working. The **Acreline Core** companion plugin (`plugins/acreline-core`) is the store-correct home for CPTs and booking REST.

## Where the money is

| Channel | What to ship | Honest limit |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **Own site** (Gumroad / Lemon Squeezy) | Full pack from `bin/build-marketplace-pack.sh` | Best margin. You set the price. |
| **ThemeForest / Envato** | Same pack: theme zip + child + Core plugin + docs + demo notes | Reviewers expect Customizer, child theme, docs, GPL assets, no dummy license. |
| **Creative Market / TemplateMonster** | Same Envato-style pack | Same presentation rules. |
| **WordPress.org** | Theme zip only. No bundled plugin. No CPTs in the theme. `readme.txt` + `screenshot.png` (1200×900) | Sage + Acorn + disabled Gutenberg will likely fail first review. Use WP.org as a **lite / traffic** listing later, or sell Core as a separate plugin. Do not claim this Sage zip is “WP.org ready” until a reviewer says so. |

Do **not** add Freemius, Envato banners, affiliate chrome, or “upgrade to Pro” nags. WP.org and ThemeForest both reject that.

## A. Plugin territory and content

**8.1 Custom post types live in Acreline Core.** `listing`, `booking`, and `agent` must not be the only thing registered in a store zip.

- Companion plugin: `plugins/acreline-core`. It defines `KEYSTONE_CORE_VERSION` and owns CPT + `keystone/v1/bookings`.
- Theme `app/post-types.php` registers the same types **only when the plugin is not loaded** (concept / live demo fallback).
- WP.org-only theme zip (future): define `KS_DISABLE_THEME_CPTS` so the theme is presentation-only. The general install / marketplace pack does **not** set this — buyers need listings without requiring the plugin.
- Switching themes must leave listing / agent / booking posts and `ks_*` meta in the database.
- Theme templates may *display* those types; they must not be required to register them.

**8.2 No hardcoded SEO / analytics overrides.** Do not add theme-options metaboxes for custom meta titles, meta descriptions, or Google Analytics / gtag snippets.

- Native fallback tags on `wp_head` are OK (`App\Support\Seo` — see `seo-native.mdc`).
- If Yoast (`WPSEO_VERSION`), Rank Math, SEOPress, or AIOSEO is active, **yield**: skip duplicate `<title>` / description / canonical / OG / Twitter.
- Do not enqueue `gtag.js` or insert GA IDs from Customizer.

This concept site still should **not** install those plugins. Yield is for buyers who do.

## B. Theme Check and WPCS

**8.3 Escape every output.**

| Kind | How |
| --- | --- |
| Text | `{{ $text }}` (Blade) or `esc_html()` |
| Attributes | `esc_attr()` |
| URLs | `esc_url()` |
| HTML copy | `{!! wp_kses_post(...) !!}` or PageCopy allow-list (`em`, `strong`, `br`, `a`) |

Do not `{!! $untrusted !!}`. REST / JSON-LD: `esc_url` on URLs; emails via `@json(...)`.

**8.4 Prefix and text domain.** Functions, hooks, constants, image sizes, and script/style handles: `keystone_`, `ks_`, `KS_`, or Acorn `App\`. Enqueue handles: `keystone-*` or `ks-*`.

- **Text domain is `acreline`** (theme slug). Sage leftovers in `vendor/` may still say `sage` — that is the one allowed extra domain (framework).
- `load_theme_textdomain( 'acreline', get_template_directory() . '/languages' )`.
- Gettext calls in theme PHP / Blade must use the literal `'acreline'` string (no PHP constant — Theme Check).

**8.5 Zero notices.** With `WP_DEBUG` true: no PHP notices/warnings, no JS `console.error` on the public site. Guard empty meta, missing query objects, and undefined JS nodes. Do not set `is_page` / `is_singular` without a real `WP_Post` (Sage 500).

## C. Demo data and licensing

**8.6 GPL-compatible assets.** Bundled JS, icons, and fonts must be GPL-compatible (MIT, Apache 2.0, SIL OFL).

- **Do not** ship Unsplash (or other stock) **files** inside `acreline.zip` unless redistribution is licensed.
- Hotlinked Unsplash (`HeroImage::DEFAULT`, blog teasers) is fine for this concept demo; for a store zip use SVG / `public/` placeholders or public-domain stills.
- Inter via Customizer / Google Fonts is OK; do not vendor a non-OFL font.
- List every bundled resource in `CREDITS.md` / `readme.txt` Resources.

**8.7 Demo import.** ThemeForest packs should let a buyer match the preview.

- **Preferred (this theme):** Tools → Seed Acreline demo / `wp ks seed`. Keep it.
- **Also ship:** `Demos/` notes + optional WXR for Tools → Import. Do **not** bundle the OCDI plugin zip inside the *theme* folder (WP.org forbids zip-in-theme). The marketplace *pack* may include XML beside the theme zip.
- Do not auto-install plugins.

## D. Footer, admin, and identity

**8.8 Credit links.** Author credit (Matt Hummel / matthummel.com) must be removable via **Appearance → Customize → Identity**. Use `rel="nofollow noopener"` on the URL. Front-end copyright is the **buyer’s site name + year**, not a locked author line.

**8.9 No admin upsells.** No dashboard nags, banner ads, Freemius, Envato, or third-party product chrome.

Allowed first-party admin (not an upsell):

- Appearance → Customize (identity, colors, typography, menus)
- Appearance → Acreline Setup (checklist of Customizer / menus / seed — dismissible)
- Appearance → Update Theme (GitHub zip)
- Tools → Seed Acreline demo + the missing-content notice (`is-dismissible`)
- Booking “advanced” confirmation notice

**8.10 WordPress menus and chrome.** Header / footer nav must use `register_nav_menus` + assigned menus when present. Hardcoded concept slugs are the **fallback** only (fresh install before seed). Buyers change menus under Appearance → Menus.

Identity (phone, email, address, hours, CTA, accent, social, demo banner) comes from `App\Support\Identity` / Customizer — not hardcoded Blade.

**8.11 Required store files.**

| File | Why |
| --- | --- |
| `style.css` headers | Theme Name, URI, Author, Description, Version, Requires at least, Tested up to, Requires PHP, License (GPLv2+), License URI, Text Domain `acreline`, Tags |
| `readme.txt` | WP.org / ThemeForest parser format |
| `screenshot.png` | 1200×900, 4:3, not an ad |
| `license.txt` | GPLv2 notice + full GPLv2 text (Theme Check) |
| `languages/acreline.pot` | Translation-ready |
| `CREDITS.md` | Third-party licenses |
| `child-theme/` | ThemeForest buyer expectation |
| `docs/marketplace/` | Buyer HTML hub (`index.html`) + seller briefs (`SELLING.md`, `themeforest-listing.md`, `wordpress-org.md`). Pack copies the hub, branding, screenshots, Customizer/listings pages, `assets/` into `Documentation/`. |

**8.12 Pack, don’t pollute the theme zip.**

- Theme zip (`bin/build-theme-zip.sh`): theme runtime only. No `.git`, no plugin zips, no `.sh` inside the theme folder. This is what buyers upload in Appearance → Themes.
- General seller pack (`bin/build-install-pack.sh`): outer `acreline-*.zip` with the theme zip + child + Core + `Documentation/` (open `index.html`). Buyers extract the outer zip; they do not upload it to WordPress.
- Marketplace folder (`bin/build-marketplace-pack.sh`) copies that pack and adds `SELLING.md` beside it for Matt. Do not put `SELLING.md`, `themeforest-listing.md`, or `wordpress-org.md` inside the buyer zip.
- `KS_DISABLE_THEME_CPTS` is for a future WP.org-only zip, not the general install pack (buyers need listings without the plugin).

## Do not

- Register CPTs in a WP.org theme zip (`KS_DISABLE_THEME_CPTS`)
- Bundle Unsplash binaries in `dist-theme/acreline.zip`
- Add theme GA / SEO metaboxes
- Leave `{!! $raw !!}` or unprefixed global functions
- Add TGMPA / Freemius / Envato admin banners
- Claim WordPress.org approval while this is still Sage + Gutenberg-off
- Hard-require a dofollow backlink
